rvices and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 6.2 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 7.1, with a 95% confidence interval of 4.4 to 11.6. December accounts for 11% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 6% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 3. Contract [1], for 14,950 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of awardees do not prove improper actions. Many contracts may be under the limit due to market prices or budget constraints, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for repeated purchases and verify if awardee A has other contracts. Review contract [1] to see if the amount was just under the limit due to fixed pricing or separate needs.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["8sIzFDPzwimkU02jNGj1Fw%3D%3D","D31gb2wdVeHua%2Fi14w%2FPLA%3D%3D","Vek4gQrSrMn%2B3JAijKO%2Bkg%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}